prompts.problem:
Let \[f(x) =
\begin{cases}
3x^2 + 2&\text{if } x\le 3, \\
ax - 1 &\text{if } x>3.
\end{cases}
\]Find $a$ if the graph of $y=f(x)$ is continuous (which means the graph can be drawn without lifting your pencil from the paper).

Find the least positive four-digit solution to the following system of congruences. \begin{align*}
7x &\equiv 21 \pmod{14} \\
2x+13 &\equiv 16 \pmod{9} \\
-2x+1 &\equiv x \pmod{25} \\
\end{align*}
